From 76ea35eaa538d9e91eaa1ae2aa9ad0d433c3ed1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyle Havlovitz <kylehav@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:46:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Show Stadium transformations in the web viewer

Add a seventh PS (unfrozen) stage button below the existing six. Keep the original PS selection frozen, preserve the selection across resets, and record the mode in exported trace metadata.

Render live collision lines for shifting platforms, walls and the rotating water-form geometry. Verify all transformation types and stable Wasm heap size, plus browser selection, reset behavior and button placement.

(cherry picked from upstream commit 77ffc009fb46a581271eb7862cab0ec23ffd3cb7 onto visual-only/04-shake)

Combined with this branch: the viewer sets the setting as bit 1 of slippiPatches (MSL_PATCH_STADIUM_TRANSFORMATIONS) next to this branch's arithmetic flags; the viewer schema is regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017JX71xgnBPBiwucag1mFRr
